# High-conversion battlefield-tour UX

Concept demo only (555 phones, `@hallowedground.test`). Forms still have to behave like a real tour-booking / lead flow.

## A. Form and input design

**Visible labels.** Never rely on `placeholder` alone. Every input / select / textarea needs a visible `<label for="id">`. Placeholder is an example (`(717) 555-0100`), not the label.

**Input types and autocomplete.** Use context-aware attributes:

| Field | Attributes |
| --- | --- |
| Phone | `type="tel"` `autocomplete="tel"` |
| Email | `type="email"` `autocomplete="email"` |
| Name | `type="text"` `autocomplete="name"` |
| Party size | `type="number"` `min` / `inputmode="numeric"` |
| Date | `type="date"` |
| Tour notes | `textarea` |

## B. Feedback and micro-interactions

Interactive actions (Book a Tour, Add to cart, contact submit, map itinerary) MUST change visually:

| State | Direction |
| --- | --- |
| Default | Gold primary / outline secondary |
| Hover | Darker gold (`--gold-300` / `--gold-800` as existing CSS) — never indigo |
| Loading | Spinner or “Sending…” + `disabled` + `aria-disabled="true"` |

In-page results MUST use `role="status"` `aria-live="polite"` (or assertive only for blocking errors).

## Do not

- Placeholder-only fields
- `hover:bg-indigo-700` / SaaS spinner kits
- Silent DOM updates after booking / cart actions
